  "title": "Publish PR reviews to GitHub Pages",
  "body": "<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\nPR reviews no longer go through VibeDrop. `comprehende export` still writes the static site. This repo publishes that folder to GitHub Pages.\n\nA pull request review lives at `pr/<number>/`. A named site lives at `site/<name>/`.\n\nReview: https://matemolnar8.github.io/comprehende/pr/67/\n\n**One-time setup.** GitHub Pages is not on for this repo yet, so that URL 404s until you enable it. In Settings, Pages, choose Deploy from a branch, branch `gh-pages`, folder `/`. The orphan `gh-pages` branch is already on origin with `.nojekyll` and this PR's export under `pr/67/`.\n\n**Cleanup.** Closing a pull request removes `pr/<n>/` only. Named sites stay until TTL. A daily workflow drops sites older than 30 days.\n\n**Agent flow.** After export, host the folder with the pages skill (`.agents/skills/pages`). Use `--pr` for a pull request review, or `--name` for anything else. Put a PR review URL in the PR body.\n\nPosted by Cursor Grok 4.6 [cursor-grok-4.6]\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-01a0960e-bf59-7deb-9dcf-caf6bfbc542f?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img alt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-01a0960e-bf59-7deb-9dcf-caf6bfbc542f&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img alt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\" src=\"https:/